BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8b39b46482eff16cc05a458fb1164ff8ed1a09b0@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261024T221536Z
DTSTART:20261025T210000Z
DTEND:20261025T230000Z
SUMMARY:Emissary Quartet: [moment]um
LOCATION:The Lilypad\, 1353 Cambridge St\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:$20 admission / $10 for students / 5pm doors / 5:30 show <a hre
 f=" class="sqs-block-button-element--small sqs-button-element--tertiary sq
 s-block-button-element" data-sqsp-button > Get Tickets Emissary Quartet’
 s debut album and concert program\, [moment]um\, is inspired by the Japane
 se concept of jo-ha-kyū\, a structure that reflects the natural flow of p
 rogression: beginning slowly (jo)\, accelerating through development (ha)\
 , and culminating in a swift and powerful conclusion (kyū). This theme of
  movement\, time\, and motion is brought to life through contemporary work
 s by living composers\, Jennifer Higdon\, Kai-Young Chan\, Sung-Hyun Yun\,
  Nicky Sohn\, Heike Beckmann\, and Herman Beeftink. Each composer uses the
  unique textures and timbres of the flute and auxiliary flutes\, to evoke 
 a sense of continuous transformation. Each piece within the album highligh
 ts various facets of moments and motion\, from the meditative\, gradually 
 unfolding soundscapes of the opening movements to the more dynamic\, rhyth
 mically intricate passages that create a palpable sense of urgency and ene
 rgy. The living composers draw upon a wide range of influences\, blending 
 minimalist repetition with more expansive\, lyrical phrasing to reflect [m
 oment]um\, while exploring the capacity of sound to depict both literal an
 d abstract forms of motion.\nhttps://www.lilypadinman.com/home/2026/10/25/
 emissary-quartet-momentum\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/bosto
 n/
URL:https://www.lilypadinman.com/home/2026/10/25/emissary-quartet-momentum
END:VEVENT
