SUMMARY:Hudson Westbrook
LOCATION:Roadrunner\, 89 Guest St\, Boston\, MA 02135
DESCRIPTION:with Special Guests KENNY WHITMIRE & ETHAN BURDICK\nHudson West
 brook is a son of Stephenville\, Texas\, baptized in Red Dirt and raised o
 n George Strait\, Turnpike Troubadours\, Parker McCollum\, Koe Wetzel\, an
 d Tracy Lawrence. After a 2024 splash debut with viral first release “Ta
 ke It Slow\,” Westbrook quickly strung together a series of grassroots h
 its while enrolled at Texas Tech University\, including debut Texas radio 
 single and chart-topper\, “Two Way Drive\,” and debut single to countr
 y radio\, “House Again.” Revitalizing the organic country he was raise
 d on while refusing to be held down by his roots\, Westbrook’s distinct 
 vocal\, “traditional country sounds and timeless songwriting” (Billboa
 rd) have become his calling card\, showcased on his self-titled EP featuri
 ng viral hits “5 to 9” and “Take Your Time.”\nhttps://www.axs.com/
 events/1513743/hudson-westbrook-tickets\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://push
 pin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.axs.com/events/1513743/hudson-westbrook-tickets
END:VEVENT
